# Deliberately NOT ignoring dist/.
#
# Consumers install by tag, e.g.
#   github:ishan-parihar/ecosystem-auth#v0.1.0
# or the equivalent archive URL. Either way the consumer receives the
# repository at that tag, so it only contains a usable package if dist/
# is committed - and there is deliberately NO `prepare` script, because npm
# runs a git dependency's lifecycle scripts in a checkout where peer
# dependencies are absent, so a tsc build there cannot resolve
# @ishan/ecosystem-core and every install from GitHub fails. Release
# builds run in CI (`npm run build`) and the dist gate proves the committed
# output matches. This mirrors @ishan/ecosystem-core, which tracks dist/ for
# the same reason.

node_modules
*.tsbuildinfo
*.tgz
.DS_Store
